{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1772650801,"nonce":"Hv12CQtFOfzi9uP4+RzGKKTCGHM=","title":"Mandible: back/forward navigation history for cross-tab deep links","message":"Audit and implement proper browser-history-compatible navigation in Mandible.\n\n## Problem\nMandible uses hash-based routing (#/tab-name), which should get browser back/forward for free when navigating between tabs. But within-tab navigation (e.g. clicking an issue link from Inbox → Issues tab with ?repo=X\u0026issue=Y params) may or may not create a browser history entry depending on whether we push a new hash or just update component state.\n\nMigrated from dotfiles issue d20728e.","files":null}]}